The North East London (NEL) Integrated Care Board (ICB) seeks a Strategic Delivery Partner to undertake a 6-month diagnostic phase that will shape the Care Closer To Home (CCTH) improvement programme.

The CCTH initiative promotes a “home first” model, aiming to:

- improve outcomes and independence for urgent and emergency care users;
- enhance efficiency and productivity;
- generate tangible and cash-releasing financial benefits for the NHS and local government across NEL; and
- address significant health inequalities and deprivation across North East London’s diverse population and promote health equity by ensuring services are inclusive, culturally competent, and accessible to all communities.

NHS Hampshire and Isle of Wight (HIOW) Integrated Care Board (ICB) and NHS Sussex ICB are seeking providers who have the capability and capacity to deliver to commission Mandatory Dental Services (MDS) on the Isle of Wight, in Bognor and Littlehampton.

The procurement is divided into Lots and providers may bid for one or more Lots from the following: 
Lot 6B1-1: Isle of Wight 
Lot 6B1-2: Bognor 
Lot 6B1-3: Littlehampton

A maximum of one contract will be awardable in each Lot, except in the case of Lot 6B1-1, where a maximum of 2 contracts will be awardable.

The aims for MDS provision are to:
