NHS Humber and North Yorkshire ICB (HNYICB) intends to undertake a Most Suitable Provider process to award a contract (without running a competitive exercise) under The Health Care Services (Provider Selection Regime) Regulations 2023 and wishes to establish a single Provider contract for the provision of a Supported Living Service in York. The service model will include a single Provider who will act as the contract holder with HNYICB. It is anticipated that the Provider will deliver the entirety of the service specification through delivery of the Supported Living element for 4 individuals at a site in York. 
 
The service will be required to:
•	Provide expertise and specialism in effectively supporting individuals with complex needs whose needs are unable to be met within existing local community provision;
•	Enhance and maintain a service user’s quality of life;
•	Support an overall reduction of admissions to hospital, hospital settings and emergency service responses;
•	Support individuals who display behaviour that significantly challenges (harm to self, other, property), including interventions to reduce behaviour challenges;
•	Respond quickly to crisis and emergency,

Contract for the Provision of ED Primary Care Services (GP Onsite Services) on behalf of University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust

A significant proportion of self-attending patients present to the Emergency Departments (ED) at UHB with conditions that are able to managed within primary care. Whilst measures are in place to re-direct many of these patients back into primary care are in action, given the absence of an Urgent Treatment Centre (UTC) on these sites, there is always likely to be the need for provision of primary care services.

The successful provider will:

• see patients after initial nurse navigation into the primary care stream, working alongside the ED team to see the right patient, in the right place, first time;

• have access to bedside and point of care testing as per national UTC specification, including Blood glucose testing, urine dip, pregnancy testing, ECG, venous blood gas testing which includes Haemoglobin, lactate and electrolytes. Where same day radiology imaging is felt to be required, access to plain film imaging is available, any other modality would be via discussion with the ED consultant;

• review patients across the full age spectrum

North of England Commissioning Support (NECS) is working for and on behalf of NHS Humber and North Yorkshire ICB, South Yorkshire ICB and West Yorkshire ICB (the Relevant Authorities) who intend to follow the Most Suitable Provider (MSP) process to award a contract for the provision of a Community Dental Service in the following Lots:

Lot 1 – West Yorkshire;
Lot 2 – North Yorkshire and York;
Lot 3 – North Lincolnshire and North East Lincolnshire;
Lot 4 – Hull and East Riding; 
Lot 5 – Sheffield; and
Lot 6 – Rotherham, Doncaster and Barnsley.

North of England Commissioning Support (NECS) is working for and on behalf of NHS England North West Public Health team (the Relevant Authority), who are managing this Competitive Process (CP) to deliver a School Aged Immunisations Service in the following areas:
• Lot 1 - Cheshire, Warrington & Wirral;
• Lot 2 - Liverpool, St Helens, Sefton, Knowsley & Halton

The Relevant Authority is issuing a Prior Information Notice (PIN) as an Expression of Interest (EOI) to engage with the market and to gain a better understanding of both the capacity and appetite of the market in delivering the proposed service.

The awarding of this contract is subject to the Health Care Services (Provider Selection Regime) Regulations 2023. For the avoidance of doubt, the provisions of the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 do not apply to this award. 

